  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation.\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n2 p x^{2}+(2 p+q) x+q=0 \\\\\r\n\\therefore D=(2 p+q)^{2}-4(2 p)(q) \\\\\r\n\\quad=4 p^{2}+q^{2}+4 p q-8 p q \\\\\r\n\\quad=4 p^{2}+q^{2}-4 p q \\\\\r\n\\quad=(2 p-q)^{2}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n$=$ a perfect square\r\nGiven equation has rational roots",
